%% Every construct this package styles, in one document. It is the coverage
%% gate's input: a construct missing from here is a construct the gate cannot
%% check, so add to this file whenever the language grows one.

= A heading

Prose with /emphasis/, *strong*, `code`, a [link](https://example.com), an
@mention, a #tag, a footnote[^note], {+inserted+}, {-deleted-}, and
more {_underlined_} text with {~struck~}, {=highlighted=}, {^super^}, {,sub,}, and {#a comment#}.

[^note]: The note's text.

== Admonitions

::: note "With a title"
Body.
:::

::: warning
Without a title.
:::

::: danger "Danger"
Body.
:::

::: tip "Tip"
Body.
:::

::: info "Information"
Body.
:::

::: success "Success"
Body.
:::

::: example "Example"
Body.
:::

::: quote "Quoted"
Body.
:::

== Quotes and figures

> A quoted line.
^ The attribution

::: figure
![First panel](image.png)
^ First panel

![Second panel](image-two.png)
^ Second panel
:::
^ The group caption

![An uncaptioned block image](wide-image.png)

== Tables

|= Column |= Another |
| cell | cell |
^ A table caption

|= Item |={>} Price |={~} Note |
| tea |{>} 3.50 | hot |

== Lists

- [ ] an open task
- [x] a done task
- [-] a dropped task
- [_] another open task
- [/] an in-progress task
- [!] a blocked task
- [>] a deferred task
- [?] a maybe task

== Code

```js
const a = 1; // <1>
```

This code block keeps its language on the code element.

